  "term": "noise_riser",
  "says": "A filtered noise riser: white noise, no tone, through a low-pass that opens over several seconds so the sound climbs from a dull rumble to full brightness - the build-up before a drop. Signature: no pitch, a flat (noisy) spectrum, the brightness rising over the held note by a large amount, level rising with it, a wide stereo image if the noise is stereo. The judge's target of the same name.",
